Grid-Bleed

Ingredients: NU JAZZ / ELECTRO JAZZ + DUB + TRIPPY, SURREAL & PSYCHEDELIC + Marimba
Creative Catalyst: It began as protest music performed on hacked traffic infrastructure.

Grid-Bleed subverts expectations by taking the organic warmth of the marimba and running it through sub-octave bass-shifters, turning the percussive wooden bars into heavy, air-shaking dub anchors rather than light melodic accents. Nu jazz brass and electric piano licks are decoupled from standard time signatures, stretched through surreal tape-delays that melt into high-voltage traffic-light hums. The result is an eerie, psychedelic dub-jazz hybrid where urban grid systems collide with hallucinatory street rhythms.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 68–82 BPM (half-time dub feel with a hyper-syncopated, swinging 5/4 or 7/8 sub-layer driven by modified traffic-relay signals).
- Harmonic Palette: Minor 11th chords, Lydian Dominant modes, detuned modal marimba clusters, and microtonal horn smears designed to mimic emergency sirens.
- Production Signatures:
  1. Opto-Capacitor Resonances: Passing low-frequency audio through physical traffic-signal relay boxes to imprint mechanical grid-hum onto jazz solos.
  2. Refractive Marimba Spatialization: An impossible technique where marimba strokes are pitch-bent using real-time spatial dopplering, making the mallets sound as if they are hitting the inside of the listener's skull from a passing vehicle.
  3. Zero-Input Dub Feedback Drool: Infinite delay loops created by routing live muted trumpets directly back into high-gain street-amplifier crossovers.
- Dynamics: Deep, seismic sub-bass drops that suddenly cut into near-silent, razor-thin glass-like marimba motifs, breathing with the unpredictable cadence of a congested metropolitan intersection.

Scene & Origin Lore
Born during the 2031 Metro Transit Strikes in sprawling industrial centers, Grid-Bleed emerged when radical jazz musicians and rogue network engineers tapped into municipal traffic cabinets, using the high-voltage relays to power illegal, low-end dub rigs. The subculture—known as "Signal-Jackers"—wears reflective hi-vis tactical coats tailored with stained-glass patches, heavy polarized welding goggles, and customized mallet holsters. Midnight gatherings occur at dead intersections where green, yellow, and red lights are override-patched to flash in time with hypnotic 808 sub-bass and reverberated marimba runs. The ritual demands absolute immersion: dancers sway in hyper-slow motion within the shifting, color-drenched neon fog, using the hacked municipal light-wash as their lightshow while traffic-camera lenses hum in forced synchronization.

- Typical Instruments: Hacked Marimba (amplified via sub-octave contact mics), Fender Rhodes (run through ring modulators), Muted Pocket Trumpet, Upright Dub-Bass, Hacked Traffic Signal Relay Controllers, Tape Delay Units, Electronic Percussion Pads.
- For Fans Of: Flying Lotus, King Tubby, Miles Davis (Cellar Door Era), Moritz von Oswald Trio.

